    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on an audit for this new fintech app we're launching. can you give me a quick checklist of the main WCAG 2.1 requirements i should be looking for regarding color contrast and screen reader compatibility? i want to make sure we don't miss anything critical before the handoff.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To ensure WCAG 2.1 compliance, when reviewing color contrast, ensure there's a contrast ratio of at least 4.5:1 between colors for normal text and background, and 7:1 for larger text, faces of buttons and links, and in-loading page content. Additionally, verify that labels and instructions are announced correctly by screen readers and that all interactive elements (like buttons and links) can be focused and accessed through keyboard navigation. Also, check for clear and consistent normalization across all screen readers.",
